{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "ibanez-ts9dx",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Ibanez TS9DX Turbo Tube Screamer (4 modes)",
  "description": "TS9DX, the four-mode Turbo Tube Screamer: the TS9 signal path (2SC1815 input buffer, TA75558 clipping stage, TA75558 tone stage, 2SC1815 output buffer) with a 4-position Mode rotary switch that changes only the clipping diodes and the 720 Hz feedback-leg capacitor, per the Ibanez TS9DX service manual and the Stompbox Electronics mode analysis. TS9 mode: two MA150 silicon diodes (1N914 class) in the feedback loop, 47 nF leg -> 615 Hz corner. '+' mode: two diodes in series each way (1.2-1.4 V threshold) and 0.22 uF -> 150 Hz. 'HOT' mode: two red LEDs with a fixed resistor across them and 1 uF -> 40 Hz, gain reduced by the resistor. 'TURBO' mode: no clipping diodes, 22 uF -> 16 Hz, so only the op-amp clips. Pots are the service-manual values: Drive 250 kA, Tone 100 kB, Level 20 kW (the 1981 TS9-style network; the TS808 file uses 500 kA / 20 kB / 100 kA). The catalogue's Bass/Mid/Treble knobs do not exist on a TS9DX and are stored only. The 2SK30A electronic bypass is omitted: the effect-on path is a closed switch.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Ibanez TS9DX service manual No.165 (Maxon, 1998), parts list and block diagram: IC1 TA75558P; Q101/105/106 2SC1815(BL); Q102/104 2SK30A; D101/102/110-113 MA150; D103/104/106 MA165; D107 RD4.7EB zener; D108 1N4002; LED1/2 TLIR124; VR1 RD9712-250KA, VR2 RD9711-100KB, VR3 RD9711-20KW; rotary mode switch SRBM1A",
      "url": "https://schematicsonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Ibanez-TS-9dx-Turbo-Tube-Screamer.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stompbox Electronics, 'The Ibanez TS9DX Modes & Their Clipping Circuits': TS9 mode = silicon pair + 47 nF (615 Hz); '+' mode = two diodes in series each way + 0.22 uF (150 Hz); HOT mode = two red LEDs with a parallel resistor + 1 uF (40 Hz); TURBO mode = no diodes + 22 uF (16 Hz)",
      "url": "https://stompboxelectronics.com/2023/04/10/the-ibanez-ts9dx-modes-their-clipping-circuits/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pedal Parts Ltd, 'Tube Screamer v2.0' build document: TS808 schematic/BOM used for the shared TS9 signal-path values (1k, 510k, 10k, 4k7, 51k, 220R, 1M, 22n, 1u, 220n, 100n, 10u, 51p, 1N914)",
      "url": "https://pedalparts.co.uk/docs/TubeScreamer2.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "R.G. Keen, 'The Technology of the Tube Screamer' (clipping stage and active tone topology)",
      "url": "http://www.geofex.com/article_folders/tstech/tsxtech.htm"
    }
  ],
  "io": {
    "input": "in",
    "output": "out",
    "inputVoltsPerFS": 1.0,
    "outputVoltsPerFS": 1.0
  },
  "oversampling": 2,
  "minRate": 176400,
  "solver": "auto",
  "multirate": {
    "oversampled": [
      "IC1A"
    ],
    "note": "Only the clipping partition (IC1A, its feedback network and the 1N914 pair) runs at 2x; the buffers and the tone stage run at the host rate with half-band converters at their exact one-way boundaries."
  },
